[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_8f65b23e23c26473\",\"r_04698e3d18eb5214\"],null,null,[[\"rc_c29ecaaa3842ea9f\",[\"### Valuation Forecasts (Year-End 2026)\\n\\nFollowing major capital events and secondary market valuations escalating from **$800 billion** in late 2025 past the **$1.0 trillion** mark, current institutional models and market analysts project SpaceX's enterprise/market valuation to settle within the following ranges by the end of 2026:\\n\\n| Scenario | Year-End Valuation Range | Implied Share Price Range | Core Underlying Drivers |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Bear Case** | **$700B – $900B** | $70 – $100 | Heavy Capex drag, severe multi-tranche lock-up supply dilution, margin compression. |\\n| **Base Case** | **$1.20T – $1.45T** | $135 – $180 | Steady Starlink free cash flow expansion, consolidated AI revenue scaling, multiple normalization. |\\n| **Bull Case** | **$1.75T – $2.10T** | $220 – $280 | Starship operationalization, accelerated direct-to-cell telecom rollouts, scarcity multiple retention. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Upside Catalysts\\n\\n1. **Starlink Cash Generation \\u0026 Direct-to-Cell Expansion**  \\n   Starlink's consumer and enterprise subscriber base continues to provide high-margin, recurring software-like revenue. The deployment of direct-to-cell capabilities via spectrum agreements enables telco-partner monetization, broadening the addressable market beyond fixed broadband.\\n\\n2. **Starship Cadence \\u0026 Commercial Readiness**  \\n   Transitioning Starship into routine payload delivery dramatically reduces cost-per-kilogram to orbit compared to Falcon 9. This unlocks rapid Starlink Gen2 deployments, high-margin NASA Artemis lunar lander milestones, and defense/national security payload contracts.\\n\\n3. **Consolidated Infrastructure \\u0026 Compute Synergies**  \\n   Integration of advanced AI compute infrastructure and cross-entity compute demand creates an additive valuation premium beyond traditional aerospace multiples, driving multiple expansion into mega-cap tech territory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Downside Risks\\n\\n1. **Lock-Up Expirations \\u0026 Float Expansion**  \\n   As early investor, employee, and insider lock-up periods expire toward the end of the year, tradable float increases substantially. The removal of float scarcity can introduce heavy institutional supply overhang and downward pricing pressure.\\n\\n2. **Capital Expenditure Intensity \\u0026 Cash Burn**  \\n   Mass-producing Starship, building orbital refueling architecture, and expanding launch facilities require immense recurring Capex. Prolonged development cycles or flight-test regulatory delays can suppress near-term margins and free cash flow yields.\\n\\n3. **Multiple Contraction \\u0026 Tech Sector Sensitivity**  \\n   Trading at forward price-to-sales multiples characteristic of high-growth tech firms leaves the valuation sensitive to broader macroeconomic interest rate pressures and regulatory scrutiny in communications and aerospace.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Sources\\n* [SatNews – SpaceX Secondary Sale and IPO Targets](https://satnews.com/2025/12/06/spacex-targets-800-billion-valuation-in-secondary-sale-eyes-2026-ipo/)\\n* [Forge Global – SpaceX Private Markets and Pre-IPO Insights](https://forgeglobal.com/insights/spacex-upcoming-ipo-news/)\\n* [Markets.com – SpaceX Valuation Models and Projections](https://www.markets.com/analysis/spacex-stock-price-prediction)\\n* [FutureSearch – SpaceX Post-Listing Fair Value Forecast](https://futuresearch.ai/spacex-ipo-valuation/)\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,[[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t3.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://satnews.com/\\u0026client\\u